<title>UK: Ford unit sets A$100 million five-year bond.</title>
<headline>Ford unit sets A$100 million five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by lead manager ABN AMRO Hoare Govett.</p>
<p> BORROWER   FORD CREDIT AUSTRALIA LTD</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  FORD MOTOR CREDIT CO</p>
<p> AMT    A$100 MLN     COUPON     7.50	MATURITY    05.DEC.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.893   PAY DATE    05.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	+34 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	A1	  LISTING    AMS/LUX   PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A+	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/AU</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC  1.50	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 12.0 PCT DUE NOVEMBER 2001 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
